WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:06.067
Welcome to Module 7 Subqueries in PostgreSQL A
subquery

00:00:06.093 --> 00:00:11.714
is a query used inside another query The important
part is not the parentheses

00:00:12.649 --> 00:00:17.227
The important part is understanding what the inner
query returns and what the outer query

00:00:17.254 --> 00:00:22.907
expects We will build this gradually starting with
result shapes and then

00:00:22.933 --> 00:00:28.631
moving through scalar subqueries membership
existence ANY and ALL correlated subqueries and

00:00:28.657 --> 00:00:34.374
derived tables Every SQL example can run directly in
the browser

00:00:35.297 --> 00:00:39.008
You can also copy the query into pgAdmin for more
practice
